rcial building products in the United States. The company distributes specialty products, including engineered wood, siding, millwork, outdoor living, specialty lumber and panels, and industrial products; and structural products, such as lumber, plywood, oriented strand boards, rebars and remesh, as well as other wood products that are used for structural support in construction projects. It provides various value-added services and solutions to customers and suppliers. The company serves national home centers, pro dealers, cooperatives, specialty distributors, regional and local dealers, and industrial manufacturers. It sells its products through warehouse sales, reload sales, and direct sales. BlueLinx Holdings Inc. was founded in 2004 and is headquartered in Marietta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Shyam K. Reddy J.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Bluelinx Holdings Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $496M market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -13% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 11% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 13% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $33M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 272.99\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2872712.7},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 56% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 26% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"BlueLinx (NYSE:BXC) and Localiza Rent a Car (OTCMKTS:LZRFY) Financial Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/bluelinx-nysebxc-and-localiza-rent-a-car-otcmktslzrfy-financial-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794397500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(BXC) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/BXC_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_111026081202_1794316322.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794316322.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BlueLinx (BXC) vs. The Competition Head-To-Head Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/bluelinx-bxc-vs-the-competition-head-to-head-survey.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794143734.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What BlueLinx (BXC) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/bluelinx-bxc-said-q3-earnings-101443439.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793873683.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"titl